@startuml OPGS - DFD Level 1 (P2, P3, P4, P5 detail)
' Online Payment Gateway Simulation - DFD Level 1
' Decomposes Level 0 processes 2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0. Each subprocess preserves
' balancing: inputs/outputs match parent Level 0 flows.
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam databaseStyle postgres

title OPGS DFD - Level 1 (detail of P2 / P3 / P4 / P5)

actor "Merchant App" as MerchantApp
actor "Customer" as Customer
actor "Administrator" as Admin
actor "Merchant Webhook\nEndpoint" as WebhookEP

' ============ P2 detail ============
package "P2 Process Payments" {
  rectangle "2.1\nAuthenticate &\nValidate Request" as P21
  rectangle "2.2\nCreate Payment\n(CREATED→PENDING)" as P22
  rectangle "2.3\nAuthorize\n(Simulation)" as P23
  rectangle "2.4\nCapture /\nFail / Expire" as P24
}
database "D1\nPayments" as D1
database "D2\nMerchants /\nAPI Keys" as D2
database "D5\nScenarios /\nRules" as D5

MerchantApp --> P21 : payment_request + Bearer\n(idempotency_key check)
P21 <--> D2 : verify test_sk_*, 401/403,\nrate-limit pre-check (429)
P21 --> P22 : valid request\n(amount>0, currency INR/USD)
P21 --> MerchantApp : 400/401/403/422\n+ correlation_id
P22 <--> D1 : insert payment + history\nunique payment_id
Customer --> P23 : checkout_input (synthetic)
P23 <--> D5 : scenario select\n(success/decline/insufficient/\nexpired/blocked/timeout) + delay
P23 --> P24 : auth verdict + code
P24 <--> D1 : AUTHORIZED→CAPTURED\nor →FAILED / →EXPIRED\n+ timestamps + reason
P24 --> MerchantApp : payment_response\n+ next_action

' ============ P4 detail (screening called by P2/P3) ============
package "P4 Fraud & Rate-Limit" {
  rectangle "4.1\nAmount Rule\nCheck" as P41
  rectangle "4.2\nVelocity\n(N / window)" as P42
  rectangle "4.3\nCountry / BIN\nMismatch Check" as P43
  rectangle "4.4\nRate-Limit\nEnforce" as P44
}
database "D6\nAudit Log" as D6

P22 --> P41 : screen new payment
P23 --> P41 : screen auth attempt
P41 --> P42 : pass (amount ok)
P42 --> P43 : pass (velocity ok)
P43 --> P44 : pass (should-check)
P44 --> P24 : allow
P41 --> P24 : fraud_risk_blocked\n(rule+timestamp → D6)
P42 --> P24 : fraud_risk_blocked
P43 --> P24 : fraud_risk_blocked
P44 --> MerchantApp : 429 + Retry-After
P44 <--> D5 : read limits/rules\n(toggle without restart)
Admin --> P44 : update rules

' ============ P3 detail ============
package "P3 Refunds & Cancellations" {
  rectangle "3.1\nValidate Eligibility\n(captured only)" as P31
  rectangle "3.2\nCreate Refund\n(full / partial)" as P32
  rectangle "3.3\nSimulate Refund\nOutcome" as P33
  rectangle "3.4\nCancel / Expire\nPayment" as P34
}
database "D3\nRefunds" as D3

MerchantApp --> P31 : refund/cancel_request
P31 <--> D1 : check state + Σ partials\n≤ captured; reject\nfailed/cancelled/fully-refunded
P31 --> P32 : eligible
P31 --> MerchantApp : 404/409/422 on ineligible
P32 <--> D3 : unique refund_id\n(idempotent replay safe)
P32 <--> D5 : refund success/fail config
P33 <--> D3 : refund_initiated→\nrefunded / refund_failed
P33 <--> D1 : captured→refund path\n(full history preserved)
P34 <--> D1 : pending→cancelled\npending→expired
P32 --> MerchantApp : refund_response

' ============ P5 detail ============
package "P5 Webhook Events" {
  rectangle "5.1\nCreate & Sign\nEvent" as P51
  rectangle "5.2\nQueue &\nDispatch" as P52
  rectangle "5.3\nRetry &\nReplay" as P53
}
database "D4\nEvents /\nWebhook Logs" as D4

P24 --> P51 : payment.authorized/\ncaptured/failed/cancelled
P33 --> P51 : refund.initiated/processed
P34 --> P51 : payment.cancelled
P51 <--> D4 : event_id, type,\ncreated_at, api_version, data\nHMAC-SHA256 sign
P51 --> P52 : signed payload
P52 --> WebhookEP : POST <1s queued,\n<2s dispatch
P52 <--> D4 : status/body/attempts/time
P52 --> P53 : on failure (≠ rollback)
P53 --> WebhookEP : exp-backoff retry\nup to max
Admin --> P53 : replay request
P53 --> MerchantApp : replayed delivery

note bottom
  Balancing: P2 in = payment_request + checkout_input; out = payment_response.
  P3 in = refund/cancel_request; out = refund_response. P5 out = webhook_event.
  Failure never corrupts payment; terminal states immutable.
end note
@enduml
